/-!
# The comparison map between a presentation and its perturbation

Let `A` be a Noetherian ring, `I ⊆ A` an ideal, `r ≥ 0` and `P = A[x₁, …, x_r]^∧`. Let
`a, b ⊆ P` be ideals with `a ⊆ b + (IP)ⁿ`. This file constructs the `A`-algebra map

`φ : P ⧸ a → P ⧸ b`,  `φ(z mod a) ≡ z mod b` modulo `(I · (P ⧸ b))^{n - (k+3)c}`,

by presenting `P ⧸ a` as an object of the category of Stacks 0AL4 carrying the tautological
completed polynomial presentation with ideal `a`, building the canonical map

`ψₙ : P ⧸ a → (P ⧸ b) ⧸ (I · (P ⧸ b))ⁿ`,  `z mod a ↦ z mod b mod Iⁿ`,

which exists exactly because `a ⊆ b + (IP)ⁿ`, and feeding `ψₙ` to the lifting lemma
`Rig.exists_algHom_lift_of_dualSituation`.

Taking `a = (g₁, …, g_m)` and `b = (g'₁, …, g'_m)` for two maps `g, g'` congruent modulo `(IP)ⁿ`,
the containment `a ⊆ b + (IP)ⁿ` is
`Rig.PerturbedPresentation.range_sup_pow_eq_of_congruentModPow`, and the resulting `φ` is the
comparison map that `Rig.PerturbedPresentation.exists_perturbationBound_algEquiv_of_algHom`
carried. The resulting isomorphism of `A`-algebras
`P ⧸ (g₁, …, g_m) ≃ₐ[A] P ⧸ (g'₁, …, g'_m)` is Stacks 0GAR,
`Rig.PerturbedPresentation.exists_algEquiv_of_perturbation`.

## Main definitions

* `Rig.PerturbedPresentation.completedPolynomialObj`: `P` as an object of Stacks 0AL4.
* `Rig.PerturbedPresentation.quotientObj` and
  `Rig.PerturbedPresentation.quotientPresentation`: `P ⧸ b` as an object of Stacks 0AL4,
  together with its tautological completed polynomial presentation, whose ideal is `b`.
* `Rig.PerturbedPresentation.compareModPow`: the map `ψₙ`.
* `Rig.PerturbedPresentation.ExtAnnihilated` and
  `Rig.PerturbedPresentation.LiftingInputs`: the hypotheses that the lifting lemma carries,
  named, so that each is written once.

## Main results

* `Rig.PerturbedPresentation.exists_comparison_algHom`: the comparison map `φ` for ideals
  `a ⊆ b + (IP)ⁿ`.
* `Rig.PerturbedPresentation.exists_comparison_algHom_of_congruentModPow`: the same for the
  ideals generated by two congruent maps `g`, `g'`.
* `Rig.PerturbedPresentation.exists_extAnnihilated_of_isRigSmooth`: the Ext-annihilation
  hypothesis, from rig-smoothness of `P ⧸ a`.

## The carried hypotheses

Nothing is assumed here beyond what the lifting lemma already carries, and those hypotheses are
passed through unchanged:

* `ExtAnnihilated A I r a c` — that `I ^ c` annihilates `Ext¹` from the completed naive
  cotangent complex of the tautological presentation of `P ⧸ a` to every `P ⧸ a`-module. For a
  rig-smooth `P ⧸ a` this holds for all large `c`; see
  `exists_extAnnihilated_of_isRigSmooth`.
* `LiftingInputs A I r b n c d q₀` — the family `dualSituation` of dual situations of Local
  Cohomology, Section 0GA6 for `P ⧸ b`, one for each thickness, with the invariants `d` and
  `q₀` independent of the thickness (`dim_eq`, `bound_eq`), together with the open duality
  input `openDuality`. The structure carries the blowup cohomology that the library does not
  build from the blowup, and `openDuality` is the section obtained by factoring through
  `can : p^*(M^∨) → (p^*M)^∨`, whose kernel and cokernel being scheme theoretically supported
  on `Y_c` is not available.
* the numeric side conditions `q₀ + (k+2)c ≤ n` and `2(k+3)c < n`, and `max(d, 1) = k + 1`.

## The precision loss

The lifting lemma concludes that `φ` agrees with `ψₙ` modulo `I^{n - (k+3)c}`, where
`max(d, 1) = k + 1`. The exponent `(k + 3) * c` is therefore the value at which the parameter
`loss` of `exists_perturbationBound_algEquiv_of_algHom` is instantiated here. Nothing is lost by
this: the integer `n` of the perturbation bound is existentially quantified, so a conclusion
reached only at `I^{n - (k+3)c}` is absorbed by taking `n` larger, which is what
`exists_algEquiv_of_perturbation` does when it enlarges the bound `n₀` to
satisfy the two numeric side conditions as well.

## Implementation notes

The two inputs beyond what was already available are the object and the presentation. `P` is an
object of Stacks 0AL4 by
`Rig.iAdicallyCompleteRing_adicCompletion_mvPolynomial_of_isNoetherianRing` and
`Rig.finiteType_quotient_adicCompletion_mvPolynomial_of_isNoetherianRing`, and `P ⧸ b` is again
one by `Rig.quotient_isAdicFiniteType`; the presentation of `P ⧸ b` with ideal `b` is the
tautological one, its comparison isomorphism being the identity. Consequently the ideal of the
presentation is `b` by definition, and no transport along an isomorphism of presentations is
needed anywhere.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GAQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GAQ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GAR](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GAR)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AJQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AJQ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AL4](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AL4)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GAI](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GAI)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory Stacks.LocalCohomology.UniformityIII

universe u v

namespace Rig.PerturbedPresentation

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard

/-! ### The extended ideal of a quotient -/

section QuotientIdeal

variable {A : Type*} [CommRing A] {T : Type*} [CommRing T] [Algebra A T]

end QuotientIdeal

/-! ### The canonical map into a quotient modulo `Iⁿ` -/

section Compare

variable {A : Type*} [CommRing A] (I : Ideal A) {T : Type*} [CommRing T] [Algebra A T]

/-- **The map `ψₙ` of the proof of Stacks 0GAR.** If `a ⊆ b + (I · T)ⁿ` then reduction modulo
`b` followed by reduction modulo `(I · (T ⧸ b))ⁿ` kills `a`, hence descends to an `A`-algebra
map `T ⧸ a → (T ⧸ b) ⧸ (I · (T ⧸ b))ⁿ`.

Indeed an element of `a` is `y + z` with `y ∈ b` and `z ∈ (I · T)ⁿ`; the first summand dies
modulo `b`, and the image of the second lies in `(I · (T ⧸ b))ⁿ` because that ideal is the
image of `(I · T)ⁿ`. -/
public def compareModPow {a b : Ideal T} {n : ℕ}
    (hab : a ≤ b ⊔ (I.map (algebraMap A T)) ^ n) :
    (T ⧸ a) →ₐ[A] ((T ⧸ b) ⧸ (I.map (algebraMap A (T ⧸ b))) ^ n) :=
  Ideal.Quotient.liftₐ a
    ((Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ A ((I.map (algebraMap A (T ⧸ b))) ^ n)).comp
      (Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ A b))
    (fun x hx => by
      obtain ⟨y, hy, z, hz, rfl⟩ := Submodule.mem_sup.mp (hab hx)
      have hmk : Ideal.Quotient.mk b (y + z) = Ideal.Quotient.mk b z := by
        rw [map_add, Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.mpr hy, zero_add]
      have hmem : Ideal.Quotient.mk b z ∈ (I.map (algebraMap A (T ⧸ b))) ^ n := by
        rw [← map_pow_quotient I b n]
        exact Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ hz
      simp only [AlgHom.comp_apply, Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ_eq_mk, hmk]
      exact Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.mpr hmem)

/-- The map `ψₙ` sends the class of `z` to the class of the class of `z`. -/
@[simp] public theorem compareModPow_mk {a b : Ideal T} {n : ℕ}
    (hab : a ≤ b ⊔ (I.map (algebraMap A T)) ^ n) (z : T) :
    compareModPow I hab (Ideal.Quotient.mk a z)
      = Ideal.Quotient.mk ((I.map (algebraMap A (T ⧸ b))) ^ n) (Ideal.Quotient.mk b z) :=
  rfl

end Compare

/-! ### `P ⧸ b` as an object of the category of Stacks 0AL4 -/

section Object

variable (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A] (I : Ideal A) (r : ℕ)

/-- The quotient `P ⧸ b` of `P = A[x₁, …, x_r]^∧`, the target of the comparison map. -/
public abbrev quotRing (b : Ideal (completedPolynomialAlgebra I r)) : Type u :=
  completedPolynomialAlgebra I r ⧸ b

/-- The ideal `I · (P ⧸ b)`. -/
public abbrev quotIdeal (b : Ideal (completedPolynomialAlgebra I r)) :
    Ideal (quotRing A I r b) :=
  I.map (algebraMap A (quotRing A I r b))

/-- `P = A[x₁, …, x_r]^∧` as an object of the category of Stacks 0AL4 over `(A, I)`: it is
`IP`-adically complete and its reduction modulo `I` is of finite type over `A ⧸ I`. -/
public def completedPolynomialObj : AdicFiniteTypeAlgebra.{u, u} A I :=
  letI : Algebra.FiniteType (A ⧸ I)
      (completedPolynomialAlgebra I r ⧸
        I.map (algebraMap A (completedPolynomialAlgebra I r))) :=
    finiteType_quotient_adicCompletion_mvPolynomial_of_isNoetherianRing A I r
  AdicFiniteTypeAlgebra.of (I := I) (completedPolynomialAlgebra I r)
    (isAdicComplete_completedPolynomialAlgebra A I r)

/-- The carrier of `completedPolynomialObj` is `P`. -/
@[simp] public theorem carrier_completedPolynomialObj :
    (completedPolynomialObj A I r).carrier = completedPolynomialAlgebra I r := rfl

/-- `P ⧸ b` is `I · (P ⧸ b)`-adically complete, being a quotient of an object of the category
of Stacks 0AL4 over a Noetherian base. -/
public theorem isAdicComplete_quotRing (b : Ideal (completedPolynomialAlgebra I r)) :
    IsAdicComplete (quotIdeal A I r b) (quotRing A I r b) :=
  (quotient_isAdicFiniteType (completedPolynomialObj A I r) b).1

/-- `P ⧸ b` as an object of the category of Stacks 0AL4 over `(A, I)`: a quotient of an object
is again an object. -/
public def quotientObj (b : Ideal (completedPolynomialAlgebra I r)) :
    AdicFiniteTypeAlgebra.{u, u} A I :=
  letI : Algebra.FiniteType (A ⧸ I) (quotRing A I r b ⧸ quotIdeal A I r b) :=
    (quotient_isAdicFiniteType (completedPolynomialObj A I r) b).2
  AdicFiniteTypeAlgebra.of (I := I) (quotRing A I r b) (isAdicComplete_quotRing A I r b)

/-- The carrier of `quotientObj` is `P ⧸ b`. -/
@[simp] public theorem carrier_quotientObj (b : Ideal (completedPolynomialAlgebra I r)) :
    (quotientObj A I r b).carrier = quotRing A I r b := rfl

/-- **The tautological completed polynomial presentation of `P ⧸ b`**: `r` variables, the ideal
`b`, and the identity as the comparison isomorphism. -/
public def quotientPresentation (b : Ideal (completedPolynomialAlgebra I r)) :
    CompletedPolynomialPresentation I (quotientObj A I r b) where
  variableCount := r
  ideal := b
  quotientEquiv := AlgEquiv.refl

/-- The number of variables of the tautological presentation is `r`. -/
@[simp] public theorem quotientPresentation_variableCount
    (b : Ideal (completedPolynomialAlgebra I r)) :
    (quotientPresentation A I r b).variableCount = r := rfl

/-- The ideal of the tautological presentation is `b`. This is what makes the tautological
presentation the right one to feed to the lifting lemma, and it holds by definition. -/
@[simp] public theorem quotientPresentation_ideal (b : Ideal (completedPolynomialAlgebra I r)) :
    (quotientPresentation A I r b).ideal = b := rfl

end Object

/-! ### The hypotheses carried by the lifting lemma -/

section Inputs

variable (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A] (I : Ideal A) (r : ℕ)

/-- **The Ext-annihilation hypothesis of Stacks 0GAQ for `P ⧸ a`.** The power `I ^ c`
annihilates `Ext¹` from the completed naive cotangent complex of the tautological presentation
of `P ⧸ a` to every `P ⧸ a`-module. For a rig-smooth `P ⧸ a` this holds for all large `c`
(`exists_extAnnihilated_of_isRigSmooth`). -/
public abbrev ExtAnnihilated (a : Ideal (completedPolynomialAlgebra I r)) (c : ℕ) : Prop :=
  ∀ x ∈ I ^ c, ∀ (N : ModuleCat.{u} (quotientObj A I r a).carrier)
    (ξ : DerivedCategory.Ext
      (DerivedCategory.Q.obj (completedNaiveCotangentComplex (quotientObj A I r a)
        (quotientPresentation A I r a)).cochainComplex)
      ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor
        (ModuleCat.{u} (quotientObj A I r a).carrier) 0).obj N) 1),
    (algebraMap A (quotientObj A I r a).carrier x) • ξ = 0

/-- **The geometric input that Stacks 0GAQ carries, for the target `P ⧸ b`.**

`dualSituation` is the family of dual situations of Local Cohomology, Section 0GA6, one for each
thickness `m`, with the invariants `d` and `q₀` independent of `m` (`dim_eq`, `bound_eq`); it
carries the blowup cohomology of Tag 0GAA, which the library does not build from the blowup.
`openDuality` is the open duality input of the library's Tag 0GAC, for every level `m ≥ n`: the
section of `p^*(M^∨)` at level `m - 2c` obtained by factoring through
`can : p^*(M^∨) → (p^*M)^∨`, whose kernel and cokernel being scheme theoretically supported on
`Y_c` is not available.

These are exactly the hypotheses `S`, `hd`, `hq₀` and `hdual` of
`Rig.exists_algHom_lift_of_dualSituation`, bundled so that they are written once. -/
public structure LiftingInputs (b : Ideal (completedPolynomialAlgebra I r)) (n c d q₀ : ℕ) where
  /-- The dual situation of Section 0GA6 at each thickness. -/
  dualSituation : ∀ m : ℕ, DualSituation (quotRing A I r b) (quotIdeal A I r b) m c
  /-- The invariant `d` does not depend on the thickness. -/
  dim_eq : ∀ m, (dualSituation m).d = d
  /-- The invariant `q₀` does not depend on the thickness. -/
  bound_eq : ∀ m, (dualSituation m).q₀ = q₀
  /-- The open duality input of Tag 0GAC, at every level `m ≥ n`. -/
  openDuality : ∀ (m e : ℕ) (_ : n ≤ m) (hem : e + 2 * c = m)
      (hq : (dualSituation m).q₀ ≤ e)
      (M : ANCModule (quotIdeal A I r b) m c)
      (ϕ : resModule (quotIdeal A I r b) m M.1 →ₗ[quotRing A I r b]
        powQuot (quotIdeal A I r b) m m),
    ∃ σ' : (dualSituation m).H M.dual 0 (e : ℤ),
      (dualSituation m).ev M e hq σ'
        = (powQuotLe (quotIdeal A I r b) (Nat.le.intro hem)).comp ϕ

end Inputs

/-! ### The Ext-annihilation hypothesis from rig-smoothness -/

section RigSmooth

/-- **The Ext-annihilation hypothesis of Stacks 0GAQ, from rig-smoothness (Stacks 0GAI).**
Rig-smoothness of `B` may be tested on any single completed polynomial presentation, so it
produces an exponent `c₀` beyond which `I ^ c` annihilates `Ext¹` from the completed naive
cotangent complex of the chosen presentation to every `B`-module. The statement is monotone in
the exponent because `I ^ c ⊆ I ^ c₀` for `c ≥ c₀`. -/
public theorem exists_extAnnihilator_of_isRigSmooth {A : Type u} [CommRing A]
    [IsNoetherianRing A] {I : Ideal A} (B : AdicFiniteTypeAlgebra.{u, v} A I)
    (Pres : CompletedPolynomialPresentation I B) (hB : IsRigSmooth B) :
    ∃ c₀ : ℕ, ∀ c ≥ c₀, ∀ x ∈ I ^ c, ∀ (N : ModuleCat.{max u v} B.carrier)
      (ξ : DerivedCategory.Ext
        (DerivedCategory.Q.obj (completedNaiveCotangentComplex B Pres).cochainComplex)
        ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{max u v} B.carrier) 0).obj N) 1),
      (algebraMap A B.carrier x) • ξ = 0 := by
  obtain ⟨c₀, hc₀⟩ := (isRigSmooth_iff B Pres).mp hB
  exact ⟨c₀, fun c hc x hx N ξ => hc₀ N ξ x (Ideal.pow_le_pow_right hc hx)⟩

variable (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A] (I : Ideal A) (r : ℕ)

/-- `ExtAnnihilated` holds for every large exponent as soon as `P ⧸ a` is rig-smooth. -/
public theorem exists_extAnnihilated_of_isRigSmooth
    (a : Ideal (completedPolynomialAlgebra I r))
    (ha : IsRigSmooth (quotientObj A I r a)) :
    ∃ c₀ : ℕ, ∀ c ≥ c₀, ExtAnnihilated A I r a c :=
  exists_extAnnihilator_of_isRigSmooth (quotientObj A I r a) (quotientPresentation A I r a) ha

end RigSmooth

/-! ### The comparison map -/

section Comparison

variable (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A] (I : Ideal A) (r : ℕ)

/-- **The interface of Stacks 0GAQ for a pair of ideals of `P = A[x₁, …, x_r]^∧`.**

Let `a, b ⊆ P` be ideals with `a ⊆ b + (IP)ⁿ`, let `I ^ c` annihilate `Ext¹` from the completed
naive cotangent complex of the tautological presentation of `P ⧸ a`, and let the invariants of
`P ⧸ b` of Local Cohomology, Section 0GA6 be carried by `L`. Then, for `n` as large as the
lifting lemma requires, there is an `A`-algebra map

`φ : P ⧸ a → P ⧸ b`  with  `φ(z mod a) - (z mod b) ∈ (I · (P ⧸ b))^{n - (k+3)c}`

for every `z ∈ P`, where `max(d, 1) = k + 1`.

The map `ψₙ` fed to the lifting lemma is `compareModPow`, which exists exactly because
`a ⊆ b + (IP)ⁿ`; the conclusion of the lifting lemma says that `φ` and `ψₙ` agree after
reduction to level `n - (k+3)c`, which is the displayed membership. -/
public theorem exists_comparison_algHom
    (a b : Ideal (completedPolynomialAlgebra I r)) (n c d q₀ k : ℕ)
    (hab : a ≤ b ⊔ (I.map (algebraMap A (completedPolynomialAlgebra I r))) ^ n)
    (hExt : ExtAnnihilated A I r a c) (L : LiftingInputs A I r b n c d q₀)
    (hk : max d 1 = k + 1)
    (hn₁ : q₀ + (k + 2) * c ≤ n) (hn₂ : 2 * ((k + 3) * c) < n) :
    ∃ φ : (completedPolynomialAlgebra I r ⧸ a) →ₐ[A] (quotRing A I r b),
      ∀ z : completedPolynomialAlgebra I r,
        φ (Ideal.Quotient.mk a z) - Ideal.Quotient.mk b z
          ∈ (quotIdeal A I r b) ^ (n - (k + 3) * c) := by
  have : IsAdicComplete (quotIdeal A I r b) (quotRing A I r b) :=
    isAdicComplete_quotRing A I r b
  obtain ⟨φ, hφ⟩ := Rig.exists_algHom_lift_of_dualSituation (quotientObj A I r a)
    (quotientPresentation A I r a) c hExt L.dualSituation d q₀ k L.dim_eq L.bound_eq hk
    n hn₁ hn₂ L.openDuality (compareModPow I hab)
  refine ⟨φ, fun z => ?_⟩
  have h : Ideal.Quotient.mk ((quotIdeal A I r b) ^ (n - (k + 3) * c))
        (Ideal.Quotient.mk b z)
      = Ideal.Quotient.mk ((quotIdeal A I r b) ^ (n - (k + 3) * c))
        (φ (Ideal.Quotient.mk a z)) :=
    DFunLike.congr_fun hφ (Ideal.Quotient.mk a z)
  exact (Ideal.Quotient.mk_eq_mk_iff_sub_mem _ _).mp h.symm

/-- **The interface of Stacks 0GAQ for a perturbed presentation.** Two maps `g, g'` congruent
modulo `(IP)ⁿ` generate ideals agreeing modulo `(IP)ⁿ`
(`range_sup_pow_eq_of_congruentModPow`), so `exists_comparison_algHom` applies and produces the
comparison map

`φ : P ⧸ (g₁, …, g_m) → P ⧸ (g'₁, …, g'_m)`

congruent to the identity modulo `(I · (P ⧸ (g'₁, …, g'_m)))^{n - (k+3)c}`. This is exactly the
map that `exists_perturbationBound_algEquiv_of_algHom` carried. -/
public theorem exists_comparison_algHom_of_congruentModPow {m : ℕ}
    (g g' : (Fin m → completedPolynomialAlgebra I r) →ₗ[completedPolynomialAlgebra I r]
      completedPolynomialAlgebra I r)
    (n c d q₀ k : ℕ)
    (hgg' : CongruentModPow (I.map (algebraMap A (completedPolynomialAlgebra I r))) g g' n)
    (hExt : ExtAnnihilated A I r (LinearMap.range g) c)
    (L : LiftingInputs A I r (LinearMap.range g') n c d q₀)
    (hk : max d 1 = k + 1)
    (hn₁ : q₀ + (k + 2) * c ≤ n) (hn₂ : 2 * ((k + 3) * c) < n) :
    ∃ φ : (completedPolynomialAlgebra I r ⧸
          (LinearMap.range g : Ideal (completedPolynomialAlgebra I r))) →ₐ[A]
        (quotRing A I r (LinearMap.range g')),
      ∀ z : completedPolynomialAlgebra I r,
        φ (Ideal.Quotient.mk (LinearMap.range g :
            Ideal (completedPolynomialAlgebra I r)) z)
          - Ideal.Quotient.mk (LinearMap.range g' :
            Ideal (completedPolynomialAlgebra I r)) z
        ∈ (quotIdeal A I r (LinearMap.range g')) ^ (n - (k + 3) * c) :=
  exists_comparison_algHom A I r _ _ n c d q₀ k
    (le_sup_left.trans
      (le_of_eq (range_sup_pow_eq_of_congruentModPow
        (I.map (algebraMap A (completedPolynomialAlgebra I r))) hgg')))
    hExt L hk hn₁ hn₂

end Comparison

end Rig.PerturbedPresentation

end
